===Hearts: 4===
<div class="mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" data-expandtext="❇ Show ❇" data-collapsetext="✖ Hide ✖">{{Hearts|4}} <div class=mw-collapsible-toggle-placeholder></div>
<div class="mw-collapsible-content">
{{HeartsTableStart}}
{{HeartsTableRow|1 = Time:|2 = 6:00 am - 6:00 pm}}
{{HeartsTableRow|1 = Map:|2 = [[Stardew:Ginger_Island#Island_West|Island West]]}}
{{HeartsTableRow|1 = Season:|2 = Any}}
{{HeartsTableRow|1 = Weather:|2 = Sunny}}
{{HeartsTableRow|1 = Conditions:| 2 = Player has reached the volcano caldera, has completed the Enchanted Grove questline, and has fixed the island farmhouse, bridge, and resort.}}
{{HeartsTableRowDesc|1 = Blink Relic|2 = The Farmer walks toward the beach south of their cabin where Lance appears from thin air and comments on the weather. Lance apologizes to the startled Farmer, saying he wishes to speak to them. He has patrolled Ginger Island for a long while before their arrival, and he's observed all the ways their work has improved the island. He's encountered many adventurers, but none quite so mysterious to him. He asks if they are familiar with magic relics.
Lance, surprised they haven't, shares that many magical artifacts are hiding around the world, and he has a few of them. He hands a magical staff called the Blink Relic over to the Farmer and says to use it to follow him to a nearby cliff. Using another relic of the same type, Lance teleports to the nearby cliff, and the Farmer follows. He comments on the view, and the camera pans over the coral reef. After, he asks if the Farmer knows about the wrecked ship on the beach. It crashed on the reef and some survivors made it onto the island.
Lance is silent for a moment, then asks whether Camilla has mentioned visiting Castle Village, and comments that Magnus has been openly speaking about the Farmer's magic talent. He ponders whether Camilla is still waiting on something, or testing the Farmer. The two use the relics to return to the beach. Lance says he doesn't need a test beyond their relic practice just now, since the Farmer used it as if they'd been doing so all along. The Farmer returns the Blink Relic to Lance, who says that whatever Camilla is up to, they'll both know soon. He says goodbye, then fades from sight.}}
{{TableEnd}}</div></div>

===Hearts: 6===
<div class="mw-collapsible mw-collapsed" data-expandtext="❇ Show ❇" data-collapsetext="✖ Hide ✖">{{Hearts|6}} <div class=mw-collapsible-toggle-placeholder></div>
<div class="mw-collapsible-content">
{{HeartsTableStart}}
{{HeartsTableRow|1 = Time:|2 = Any}}
{{HeartsTableRow|1 = Map:|2 = [[Highlands Outpost|Highlands Outpost]]}}
{{HeartsTableRow|1 = Season:|2 = Any}}
{{HeartsTableRow|1 = Weather:|2 = Any}}
{{HeartsTableRow|1 = Conditions:|2 = Player has unlocked the Highlands zone.}}
{{HeartsTableRowDesc|1 = Monster Studies|2 = The Farmer walks up to the Highland Outpost Tower. Lance, who stands on top of the tower, notices the farmer, welcomes them and tells them to come to him. Lance explains, how the magical wards that surround the tower inflict a shock on approaching monsters and cause them to turn away from the Outpost.
Lance proceeds to ask the farmer if they were willing to help him with a field study he wishes to conduct. The farmer shows excitement and Lance casts a spell on both of them in order to prevent monsters from noticing them. Together Lance and the farmer observe the behaviour of a variety of monsters in the wild, untouched by human interference. The monsters are shown to peacefully coexist with each other and their environment.
The trip through the Highlands ends in the Highlands Cavern, where Lance explains that he suspects that the key to understanding the origins of the Cave lie in the Gemfish that live in the nearby body of water. However Lance has to admit, that so far he has been unable to catch one and claims that only an experienced angler could catch a Gemfish. Shortly afterwards the protection spell, that had shielded Lance and the Farmer thus far, runs out and in the face of approaching danger, Lance teleports both of them back to the Outpost.
Lance thanks the farmer for their help and tells them, that he hopes the farmer learned something new during the day.}}
{{TableEnd}}</div></div>

